  @doc ~S"""
  Returns a [`Locator`](`PlaywrightEx.Locator`) object pointing to the same `iframe` as this frame locator.

  Useful when you have a [`FrameLocator`](`PlaywrightEx.FrameLocator`) object obtained somewhere, and later on would like to interact with the `iframe` element.

  For a reverse operation, use `PlaywrightEx.Locator.content_frame/1`.

  **Usage**

  ```js
  const frameLocator = page.locator('iframe[name="embedded"]').contentFrame();
  // ...
  const locator = frameLocator.owner();
  await expect(locator).toBeVisible();
  ```
  """
  @spec owner(t()) :: PlaywrightEx.Locator.t()
  def owner(frame_locator) do
    PlaywrightEx.Client.FrameLocator.owner(frame_locator)
  end
end
